        ":question/problem": "What is $\\displaystyle \\int(\\frac{1}{3 + x} + \\frac{1}{3 - x})dx$?",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{3 + x}+\\frac{1}{3 - x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{3 + x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{3 - x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|3 + x|-\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|3 - x|+C \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|\\frac{3 + x}{3 - x}|+\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|\\frac{3 + x}{3 - x}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm.",
