        ":question/problem": "Calculate $\\int (\\frac{1}{4+8x}+\\frac{1}{4-8x})\\,\\text{d}x.$ Assume that $K$ is an arbitrary positive constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's solve this using the general formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int (\\frac{1}{4+8x}+\\frac{1}{4-8x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{4+8x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{1}{4-8x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|4+8x|-\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|4-8x|+C \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|\\frac{4+8x}{4-8x}|+\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061K \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(K|\\frac{4+8x}{4-8x}|)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we used the laws of logarithms to write the result as a single logarithm.",
